{"availability":"available","full":"moose25/world-cup-2026-readme-widget","name":"world-cup-2026-readme-widget","description":"Embeddable, self-updating FIFA World Cup 2026 panels for your README, website, or dashboard - live match, group standings, and a Round-of-32 qualification tracker for the new 48-team format. Real flags, no API key.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":9,"forks":1,"created":"2026-05-27T20:43:09Z","updated":"2026-06-17T19:28:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wc26-widget.vercel.app","topics":["badge","dashboard","embed","fifa","football","github-readme","home-assistant","iframe","openfootball","profile-readme","readme","readme-widget","serverless","soccer","svg","vercel","widget","world-cup","world-cup-2026","worldcup"],"demo":"https://wc26-widget.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T09:43:59.257Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T09:43:59.257Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T09:43:59.257Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T09:43:59.257Z","stars":9,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Self-updating FIFA World Cup 2026 panels you can drop into any GitHub README, website, or wiki, with one line of Markdown. Countdown, live match, group standings, and the only Round-of-32 qualification tracker that handles the new 48-team format. Real country flags, no API key, no account, no JavaScript, just -able SVG.","Built on the free, public-domain openfootball dataset. Kickoff times convert to your timezone. Light and dark themes included. ▶ Live demo + embed builder: pick a panel, team, and timezone, then copy the snippet. ⚠️ The hosted wc26-widget.vercel.app is a limited demo — heavily cached and rate-limited, so it can lag and may pause under load. To get the full tool (always-fresh panels that won't go down), deploy your own free copy in 2 minutes and embed that URL. It's the intended way to use the widget."],"features":["Countdown: